# TaskFence environment template (Phase 1).
#
# Copy to .env and fill in only what you need. The local demo works with every
# value below left at its default. No secrets belong in this file or in source.
#
# Configuration is read and validated in taskfence/config.py. Invalid or
# contradictory values fail at startup instead of falling back to a default.

# --- Gateway ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the agent-side GatewayClient connects.
TASKFENCE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- Persistence -----------------------------------------------------------
# PostgreSQL URL. When set, it must be postgresql:// or postgres://.
# Leave unset for the local SQLite demo.
# TASKFENCE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/taskfence
#
# SQLite file used when TASKFENCE_DATABASE_URL is unset.
TASKFENCE_DB=taskfence.sqlite3

# --- Identity --------------------------------------------------------------
# local = explicit local principal (demo). jwt = verified bearer tokens only.
# The mode is fixed for the process lifetime: it is decided at startup and is
# never downgraded at runtime. A bad enabled-mode configuration fails startup
# instead of falling back to legacy authentication.
TASKFENCE_AUTH_MODE=local
#
# Required when TASKFENCE_AUTH_MODE=jwt. Setting these while the mode is
# 'local' is rejected rather than silently downgrading to anonymous access.
# TASKFENCE_AUTH0_ISSUER=https://YOUR_TENANT/
# TASKFENCE_AUTH0_AUDIENCE=YOUR_API_AUDIENCE
#
# Phase 3 (G-04) JWT verification. TASKFENCE_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY is the SINGLE
# configured PEM public key (public material, not a secret); there is no JWKS
# and no key rotation in this phase. TASKFENCE_JWT_ALLOWED_ALGS is the fixed
# algorithm allowlist (default RS256); 'none' is always rejected. The issuer
# and audience fall back to the Auth0 values above when not set separately.
# Required claims: iss, aud, sub, exp, iat, jti.
#
# Setting any of the three variables below while TASKFENCE_AUTH_MODE is 'local'
# is a startup ERROR: security settings are never silently ignored. A
# multi-line PEM does not survive a quoted one-line value, so export it from
# the key file:
#
#   export TASKFENCE_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY="$(cat /path/to/jwt-public.pem)"
#
# TASKFENCE_JWT_PUBLIC_KEY=
# TASKFENCE_JWT_ALLOWED_ALGS=RS256
# TASKFENCE_JWT_ISSUER=https://YOUR_TENANT/
# TASKFENCE_JWT_AUDIENCE=YOUR_API_AUDIENCE
#
# Phase 3 (G-04): the DASHBOARD process needs a reviewer access token from the
# configured issuer/audience to call the two protected approval endpoints while
# the gateway is in JWT mode. It is attached server-side as
# `Authorization: Bearer ...`, never rendered or logged, never sent to the
# browser. JWT mode has no in-dashboard login flow yet and is NOT demo-ready:
# see docs/implementation/PHASE_3_JWT_READINESS.md.
# TASKFENCE_REVIEWER_JWT=

# --- Models ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Local regression/demo path.
TASKFENCE_OLLAMA_URL=http://localhost:11434
TASKFENCE_MODEL=qwen3
#
# Cloud provider (Phase 8). No model name is assumed: set GEMINI_MODEL before
# enabling the provider. Free-tier keys are for synthetic/demo data only.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=

# --- Timeouts (seconds) ----------------------------------------------------
TASKFENCE_CHAT_TIMEOUT=60
TASKFENCE_MCP_TIMEOUT=30

# --- Optional shared accounting (Phase 7) ----------------------------------
# UPSTASH_REDIS_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_TOKEN=

# --- Messaging -------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset keeps the deterministic JSONL fake sink. When set, the gateway still
# performs at most one POST, and only on an ALLOW path.
# TASKFENCE_REAL_SLACK_WEBHOOK=

# --- Human approval / administration --------------------------------------
# Required for approval detail and resolution endpoints. The agent side never
# holds this value. Generate a unique value locally; never commit it.
# TASKFENCE_ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- Risk/budget defaults (configured here; enforced from Phase 7) ---------
TASKFENCE_BUDGET_MAX_TOOL_CALLS=50
TASKFENCE_BUDGET_MAX_OUTBOUND_CALLS=20
TASKFENCE_BUDGET_MAX_RECORDS_READ=1000
TASKFENCE_BUDGET_MAX_OUTBOUND_MESSAGES=20
TASKFENCE_BUDGET_MAX_MODEL_TURNS=8
TASKFENCE_BUDGET_MAX_EXECUTION_SECONDS=300
# 0 means "not configured". Do not claim a data-volume budget is enforced at 0.
TASKFENCE_BUDGET_MAX_DATA_BYTES=0
